A directory that declares no `struct Frontmatter` gets one synthesized from
the union of the keys its pages wrote, in the order they were first seen, each
typed by its YAML scalar and defaulting to that type's zero. So `draft` is a
bool on every page although only `notes.md` wrote it, and `index.md` shows
`false` for it.

deny * `innerHTML` -- a page is a component tree; nothing is handed to a parser at run time

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"
import docs "md:./docs"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
}

docs.site {
    component layout(page, content) {
        ui.window(title=page.frontmatter.title, href=page.href) {
            ui.text(value="draft {page.frontmatter.draft}")
            content
        }
    }
}
-- docs/index.md --
---
title: Home
---

Home.
-- docs/notes.md --
---
title: Notes
draft: true
---

Notes.
-- out/none/html/index.html --
